## Why This Is Asked

Interviews often test real-time data engineering and AI integration skills. This question probes how the candidate designs end-to-end streaming pipelines, strong privacy controls, reliable error handling, and cost-aware architecture using AWS AI services.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time streaming: Kinesis Data Streams and Lambda
- AI processing: Amazon Comprehend, SageMaker endpoint
- Data storage and protection: S3 versioning, SSE-KMS
- State and queries: DynamoDB index
- Reliability and cost: DLQ, backpressure, shard sizing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Lambda handler sketch
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const comprehend = new AWS.Comprehend();
const sagemaker = new AWS.SageMakerRuntime();

exports.handler = async (event) => {
  for (const rec of event.Records) {
    const msg = JSON.parse(Buffer.from(rec.kinesis.data, 'base64').toString());
    const { Text } = msg;
    const sit = await comprehend.detectSentiment({ Text, LanguageCode: 'en' }).promise();
    const kp = await comprehend.detectKeyPhrases({ Text, LanguageCode: 'en' }).promise();
    const resp = await sagemaker.invokeEndpoint({ EndpointName: 'ComplianceClassifier', Body: JSON.stringify({ text: Text }), ContentType: 'application/json' }).promise();
    // Persist and upsert logic omitted for brevity
  }
};
```

